    "title": "Autaxys Ontological Closure: When Is a Physical Quantity Computationally Real?",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21747701",
    "publication_date": "2026-08-01",
    "description": "Version 1.0 \u2014 2026-08-01. Operational criterion for physical reality: a quantity is physically real only if there exists a finite Turing-machine protocol that approximates it with a computable modulus of convergence, yielding measurement-distinguishable predictions. Decomposes into 11 sub-claims across quantum foundations, cosmology, thermodynamics, information theory, and computability theory.",
